Installing Portare BIOS from Android

- Copy the portareos_abl folder from the SD card to the root of Android's
  internal storage.
- As root, run backup_abl.sh from there. It saves your current bootloader
  as abl_a.img and abl_b.img in the same folder.
- Then, as root, run flash_abl.sh to install Portare BIOS.
- Restart. PortareOS starts first, from internal storage if it's installed
  there, otherwise from the SD card.
- To open Portare BIOS, hold Volume Down while powering on. Boot starts any
  system once; Boot order sets which one starts first.
- Install PortareOS copies PortareOS from the SD card to internal storage,
  next to Android (Dualboot) or in its place (Replace Android).
- To go back, run restore_backup_abl.sh as root.
